":"nigel-scullion","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Migration Amendment (Abolishing Detention Debt) Bill 2009 [No. 2] - Third Reading - Read a third time","noes":29,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2009-09-08.13.1) to read the bill a third time. This means that the bill is now passed in the Senate and, as it has already passed in the House of Representatives, it will now become law. The purpose of the bill was to change the law so that asylum-seekers will no longer be charged for their upkeep when locked up in detention centres. _Debate in Parliament_ The Coalition voted against reading the bill for a third time, with the exception of Liberal Senator [Judith Troeth](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Judith_Troeth&mpc=Senate&house=senate). Senator Troeth [crossed the floor](http://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/crossing-the-floor.html) to vote in favour of the bill.(Read more about Senator Troeth's rebellion [here](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2009-09-08/liberal-crosses-floor-to-end-detainee-debt/1421372). ) _Background to the bill_ The [bill](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r4157) was introduced by Labor MP [Laurie Ferguson](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Laurie_Ferguson&mpc=Reid&house=representatives) to amend the _Migration Act 1958_. It removes the liability for immigration detention and related costs for certain persons and liable parties and extinguish all outstanding immigration detention debts. In other words, people detained in immigration detention will no longer be charged the cost of their detention.(Read more about this amendment on [Lawyers Weekly](http://www.lawyersweekly.com.au/news/detention-debt-for-refugees-scrapped) and [News.com.au](http://www.news.com.au/national/senate-passes-legislation-abolishing-asylum-seeker-debt/story-e6frfkp9-1225770631177).) References","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1704","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2009-09-08/1"}
